{"guid": "N62_001", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "strategic_tactic", "concept_label": "gambit (chess)", "concept_definition": "In chess, a gambit is an opening in which a player offers material, usually a pawn, to gain a positional or developmental advantage.", "translations": {"en": "gambit", "lt": "gambitas", "zh": "弃兵开局", "fr": "gambit", "es": "gambito", "es-419": "gambito"}, "difficulty_level": 1202, "disambiguation": {"en": "chess"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N62_002", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "strategic_tactic", "concept_label": "sacrifice (chess)", "concept_definition": "In chess, a sacrifice is the deliberate giving up of a piece or pawn to gain a positional, tactical, or material advantage.", "translations": {"en": "sacrifice", "zh": "弃子", "fr": "sacrifice", "es": "sacrificio", "es-419": "sacrificio"}, "difficulty_level": 1202, "disambiguation": {"en": "chess"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N62_003", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "strategic_tactic", "concept_label": "fork (chess)", "concept_definition": "In chess, a fork is a move that makes one piece attack two or more opposing pieces at the same time.", "translations": {"en": "fork", "zh": "双重攻击", "fr": "fourchette", "es": "ataque doble", "es-419": "ataque doble"}, "difficulty_level": 1202, "disambiguation": {"en": "chess"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N62_004", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "strategic_tactic", "concept_label": "skewer (chess)", "concept_definition": "In chess, a skewer is an attack on a valuable piece that forces it to move, exposing a less valuable piece behind it to capture.", "translations": {"en": "skewer"}, "difficulty_level": 1202, "disambiguation": {"en": "chess"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N62_005", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "strategic_tactic", "concept_label": "fianchetto", "concept_definition": "In chess, a fianchetto is a development in which a bishop is placed on the long diagonal by first moving the pawn in front of the knight one square and then moving the bishop to the resulting diagonal.", "translations": {"en": "fianchetto", "lt": "fiančetas", "fr": "fianchetto", "es": "fianchetto", "es-419": "fianchetto"}, "difficulty_level": 1202, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N62_006", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "strategic_tactic", "concept_label": "fast break (basketball)", "concept_definition": "A quick basketball attack in which a team moves the ball toward the opponent’s basket before the defense has time to get set.", "translations": {"en": "fast break", "zh": "快攻", "fr": "contre-attaque rapide", "es": "contraataque rápido", "es-419": "contraataque rápido"}, "difficulty_level": 1201, "disambiguation": {"en": "basketball"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N62_007", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "strategic_tactic", "concept_label": "alley-oop", "concept_definition": "In basketball, an alley-oop is a play in which a player throws the ball near the basket for a teammate to catch in the air and score, usually with a dunk.", "translations": {"en": "alley-oop", "zh": "空中接力", "fr": "alley-oop", "es": "alley-oop", "es-419": "alley-oop"}, "difficulty_level": 1201, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N62_008", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "strategic_tactic", "concept_label": "screen (basketball)", "concept_definition": "In basketball, a screen is a player's position that blocks a defender's path so a teammate can get free.", "translations": {"en": "screen", "zh": "掩护", "fr": "écran", "es": "bloqueo", "es-419": "bloqueo"}, "difficulty_level": 1201, "disambiguation": {"en": "basketball"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N62_009", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "strategic_tactic", "concept_label": "pick and roll", "concept_definition": "In basketball, a play in which one player sets a screen for a teammate with the ball, then moves toward the basket to receive a pass.", "translations": {"en": "pick and roll", "zh": "挡拆", "fr": "pick-and-roll", "es": "bloqueo y continuación", "es-419": "bloqueo y continuación"}, "difficulty_level": 1201, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N62_010", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "strategic_tactic", "concept_label": "sledging", "concept_definition": "In cricket, sledging is the use of verbal remarks or insults by players to distract, intimidate, or unsettle an opponent.", "translations": {"en": "sledging"}, "difficulty_level": 1206, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
{"guid": "N62_011", "pos_type": "noun", "pos_subtype": "strategic_tactic", "concept_label": "blitz (American football)", "concept_definition": "A defensive tactic in American football in which extra defenders rush the quarterback to pressure or tackle him.", "translations": {"en": "blitz", "fr": "blitz", "es": "blitz", "es-419": "blitz"}, "difficulty_level": 1207, "disambiguation": {"en": "American football"}, "sense_prominence": "rare"}
